# Negative test (issue #113): a genuinely non-positive constructor argument
# is rejected with an accurate error naming the argument.
# The family Bad occurs in the *domain* of k's type, so this is not
# strictly positive and must be rejected (contrast 19-higher-order-session.ep,
# where the family occurs only in codomains).

data Bad : ? where
| bad (k : (Bad -> Bad) -> Bad) : Bad
